- What are the time complexities for insert, erase, and query operations?
- How would you extend this to support minimum queries or range sum queries?

## Complexity Analysis
- **Time**: O(log N) per insertInterval, eraseInterval, and queryGlobalMax, where N is the coordinate domain size (2^31)
- **Space**: O(k log N) where k is the number of active intervals, since only nodes touched by operations are created (sparse representation)

## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of order-statistics structures, coordinate compression, and practical trade-offs for large domains in a beginner-friendly way.

## Key Concepts
- Fenwick tree (BIT) for prefix sums
- Coordinate compression to handle sparse domains
- kth-order statistics via prefix sums
- Merge strategy: small-to-large to reduce work

## Code Example
```javascript
class Fenwick {
  constructor(n) {
    this.n = n;
    this.f = new Array(n + 1).fill(0);
  }
  add(i, delta) {
    for (; i <= this.n; i += i & -i) this.f[i] += delta;
  }
  sum(i) {
    let s = 0;
    for (; i > 0; i -= i & -i) s += this.f[i];
    return s;
  }
  kth(k) {
    let idx = 0;
    let bit = 1;
    while ((bit << 1) <= this.n) bit <<= 1;
    for (let d = bit; d > 0; d >>= 1) {
      const next = idx + d;
      if (next <= this.n && this.f[next] < k) {
        idx = next;
        k -= this.f[next];
      }
    }
    return idx + 1;
  }
}
```

